// Two of Pixie's Ascension lines that react to ANY of her explosions (Bunny Bomb, dash bombs,
// explosive weapons) rather than one specific mechanic - see DemolitionMasteryUtility.cs/
// PixieDemolitionMasterySystem.cs and the OnExplosionCriticalHit/OnAreaExplosionDetonated signals in
// Combat.qtn. Concussive Force and Volatile Payload (the other two traits this batch used to hold)
// were removed - Concussive Force's knockback was folded into Direct Hit's own rank 3 (see
// DirectHitUpgrade below); Volatile Payload was dropped entirely, not merged anywhere.
//
// Pocket Bombs is deliberately NOT named/shaped like ClusterBombUpgrade (see Heroes/Pixie/
// ClusterBombSkillAction.cs) - that's a different, pre-existing Hero Skill Upgrade (deterministic
// Projectile-based bomblet count from Bunny Bomb specifically) and must not be confused with or
// touched by this trait, which is a chance-based Mini Bomb drop from any qualifying explosion.

// Direct Hit - a binary "inner zone" bonus: within InnerRadiusFraction of an explosion's own radius,
// damage is multiplied by 1 + DamageMultiplierBonus. Read live in DemolitionMasteryUtility.
// ApplyProximityEffects, never baked into CharacterStats. At rank 3, HasKnockback additionally
// applies an arcade-style knockback falloff to the same inner-zone hits (folded in from the old
// standalone Concussive Force ascension) - full KnockbackForce out to InnerRadiusFraction, then a
// linear taper to 0 at the blast edge; KnockbackEliteMultiplier further scales the result against
// Elite-tier enemies (<1, reduced effect) - Bosses need no dedicated handling here at all,
// TierStats.CanBeInterruptedByKnockback/KnockbackMultiplier already resist the displacement itself.
component DirectHitUpgrade
{
    FP InnerRadiusFraction;
    FP DamageMultiplierBonus;
    Boolean HasKnockback;
    FP KnockbackForce;
    FP KnockbackUpwardForce;
    FP KnockbackEliteMultiplier;
}

// Pocket Bombs (the design's own "Cluster Charges" trait name - kept distinct here on purpose, see
// this file's own header comment) - any qualifying explosion (see OnAreaExplosionDetonated, fired
// once per genuine radius blast, never from a Mini Bomb's own detonation) rolls Chance to drop a
// stationary Mini Bomb at the blast center dealing DamagePercent of Bunny Bomb's own base damage (see
// PixieAscensionUtility.ResolveBunnyBombDamage) - not a flat value, so it scales with Pixie's skill
// scaling. Explosion's own AreaHitData.BlastRadius is what actually makes this smaller than the
// parent blast.
component PocketBombsUpgrade
{
    FP Chance;
    FP DamagePercent;
    FP Fuse;
    AssetRef<EntityPrototype> MiniBombPrototype;
    AssetRef<AreaHitData> Explosion;
}
